---
import TextPage from '~/layouts/TextPage.astro';
import { CONTACT, ANALYTICS, CHAT } from '~/config/site';

const path = '/cookie-policy/';
const analyticsActive = Boolean(ANALYTICS.ga4 || ANALYTICS.gtm);
const chatActive = Boolean(CHAT.zendeskKey);
---

<TextPage
  title="Cookie Policy | Cone Sleeves UK"
  description="What cookies and tracking technologies conesleeves.co.uk uses, described accurately rather than as a generic template."
  path={path}
  h1="Cookie Policy"
  standfirst="What this website actually sets, described from how it is configured rather than from a template."
  updated="2026-08-13"
  crumbLabel="Cookie Policy"
>
  {
    chatActive && (
      <>
        <h2>Live Chat Sets Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site loads Zendesk Chat so you can talk to us during the working day. Zendesk
          sets cookies in your browser to keep a conversation attached to you as you move
          between pages, to remember whether the chat window is open, and to reconnect you
          to the same conversation if you return.
        </p>
        <p>
          These are set by Zendesk rather than by us, and they are governed by Zendesk's own
          privacy terms as well as this policy. They are not used for advertising.
        </p>
        <p class="pending">
          <strong>This section needs completing before launch</strong>
          Zendesk's current cookie names, their individual purposes and their lifetimes have
          not been listed here, because they should be taken from Zendesk's own published
          documentation rather than guessed at. A consent mechanism is also outstanding: the
          chat widget loads on page load today, and non-essential cookies should be set only
          after a visitor agrees.
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }

  {
    !analyticsActive && (
      <>
        <h2>No Analytics or Advertising Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Beyond live chat, conesleeves.co.uk sets no cookies of its own, no analytics
          cookies, and no advertising or tracking cookies. No analytics tag, tag manager,
          advertising pixel or session-recording script is loaded on any page.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is a statement about how the site is configured rather than a promise about
          the future. It will stop being accurate the moment a tag is switched on, which is
          why the section below sets out what has to happen if one is.
        </p>

        <h2>What the Site Itself Stores</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing in your browser. The site's own code uses no local storage, no session
          storage and no fingerprinting. Fonts and images are served from this domain rather
          than from a third-party network, so browsing the pages themselves sends no request
          elsewhere.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our server records the IP address of enquiry form submissions briefly, in order to
          apply a rate limit against automated spam. That is a server-side log rather than
          anything placed on your device.
        </p>

        <h2>If Analytics Is Added Later</h2>
        <p>
          The site is built so that Google Analytics or Google Tag Manager can be switched on
          through configuration. If that happens, three things must happen with it:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            This page must be updated to name the cookies actually set, what each one does
            and how long it lasts.
          </li>
          <li>
            A consent mechanism must be added, so non-essential cookies are only set after a
            visitor agrees.
          </li>
          <li>
            The tag must be loaded only after that consent is given, rather than on page
            load.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="pending">
          <strong>Pre-launch note</strong>
          No analytics identifier has been configured for this site, and none has been
          invented. If tracking is enabled before launch, the three steps above are
          outstanding work rather than optional extras.
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }

  {
    analyticsActive && (
      <>
        <h2>Analytics Is Enabled on This Site</h2>
        <p>
          An analytics tag is currently configured, which sets cookies in your browser to
          measure how the site is used.
        </p>
        <p class="pending">
          <strong>This section needs completing</strong>
          Now that a tag is configured, this page must list each cookie it sets, its purpose
          and its lifetime, and a consent mechanism must gate it. Until that is done, this
          policy does not accurately describe the site.
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }

  <h2>Third Parties</h2>
  <p>
    The WhatsApp buttons on this site open WhatsApp, which is operated by a third party
    with its own cookies and privacy terms. Following that link takes you outside this
    website and outside this policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    Zendesk, which provides the chat window, is a third party processing what you type in
    that window on our behalf. Anything you send through chat reaches Zendesk as well as
    us.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If anything here does not match what you observe in your browser, we would genuinely
    like to know — write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    See also our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for how enquiry details are
    handled.
  </p>
</TextPage>
